{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTraceLaw","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTraceLaw","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace"],"declarations":41,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.TwoSidedImpliesDisjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.TwoSidedImpliesDisjoint","kind":"def","line":715,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L715-L725","doc":"**A statement of what remains, so the gap is in the file rather than only in\nthe bean.**\n\n`TwoSidedMarkov T → DisjointBlockMultiplicative T` is what `qou-301d` wants. It\nis *not* proved here, and the obstruction is stated in the module docstring: an\n`Algebra.adjoin` induction does not close the multiplicative step. This\ndefinition names the target so a later proof has something to attack and so the\nabsence is visible to a reader of the Lean rather than only to a reader of the\nbean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.towerSpan_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.towerSpan_unit","kind":"instance","line":688,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L688-L713","doc":"**Anti-vacuity: `TowerSpan` is inhabited**, so no theorem above is vacuously\ntrue.\n\n🛑 **But read this as a DEGENERATE witness, and it is the weakest kind.** In\n`unitMarkovTrace` the algebra *is* `R`, so every submodule containing `1` is\nalready `⊤` and the step condition holds for a reason that has nothing to do with\ntower structure. Worse, its filtration is constant, so `towerSpan_of_constant`\nabove already covers it: the witness exercises **none** of what `TowerSpan`\nasserts.\n\n**No witness with a growing filtration is supplied here**, and building one\nessentially means constructing a Hecke or group-algebra tower — which Mathlib\ndoes not have (see `OcneanuTrace`'s measured note: one hit for \"Hecke\", a\nbibliography title). Until such a witness exists, `TowerSpan` should be read as a\n*well-posed statement of the classical structure theorem*, not as a hypothesis\ndemonstrated to be satisfiable in any interesting case. Bean `qou-301d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.towerSpan_of_constant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.towerSpan_of_constant","kind":"theorem","line":671,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L671-L686","doc":"**Any tower whose filtration does not GROW satisfies `TowerSpan` for free.**\n\nThis is stated to make the weakness of the anti-vacuity witness below *precise\nand machine-checked*, rather than leaving it as prose. If `shiftedUpTo n (M+1) ≤\nshiftedUpTo n M` then the step condition is discharged by `le_sup_left` alone,\nusing nothing about sandwiches, nothing about `g (M+1)`, and nothing about the\ntower.\n\nSo the entire content of `TowerSpan` lies in towers whose filtration genuinely\ngrows — and a witness that does not grow is evidence of satisfiability only, not\nof the hypothesis being reasonable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.disjointBlock_of_towerSpan","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.disjointBlock_of_towerSpan","kind":"theorem","line":657,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L657-L669","doc":"**The reduction, stated as the implication it is.** With the tower structure\nhypothesis and the quadratic relation, the disjoint-block law holds — for every\n`b ∈ shifted n`, repeated top-level generators included, so this DOES reach the\natom word.\n\n🛑 It reaches it *conditionally*. `TowerSpan` has no Hecke instance here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.mem_shiftedUpTo_of_mem_shifted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.mem_shiftedUpTo_of_mem_shifted","kind":"theorem","line":640,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L640-L655","doc":"`shifted n` is the directed union of its filtration stages. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_shiftedUpTo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_shiftedUpTo","kind":"theorem","line":627,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L627-L638","doc":"The law on every filtration stage, by induction on the level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_shiftedUpTo_base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_shiftedUpTo_base","kind":"theorem","line":611,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L611-L625","doc":"The base level collapses to one generator's subalgebra, where\n`tr_mul_adjoin_gen` applies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.TowerSpan.step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.TowerSpan.step","kind":"theorem","line":607,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L607-L607","doc":"One filtration step is spanned by the previous stage plus single sandwiches. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.TowerSpan.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.TowerSpan.mk","kind":"ctor","line":605,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L605-L605","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.TowerSpan","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.TowerSpan","kind":"class","line":600,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L600-L609","doc":"**The tower structure hypothesis — the one input that remains.**\n\nEach filtration step is spanned by the previous stage together with single\nsandwiches. For the Iwahori-Hecke tower this is `H (m+1) = H m + H m · g m · H m`;\nit is classical and it is **not proved here**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.shiftedUpTo_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.shiftedUpTo_mono","kind":"theorem","line":594,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L594-L598","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.shiftedUpTo_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.shiftedUpTo_le","kind":"theorem","line":588,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L588-L592","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.shiftedUpTo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.shiftedUpTo","kind":"def","line":584,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L584-L586","doc":"The level-`≤ M` part of `shifted n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_step","kind":"theorem","line":551,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L551-L582","doc":"**The inductive step, and the mathematical content of this section.** If the\nlaw holds on `B`, it holds on `B` extended by one sandwiched generator.\n\n`markov₂_of_markov` is what does the work — and it is free, per the correction\nat the top of this file. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.sandwich","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.sandwich","kind":"def","line":547,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L547-L549","doc":"One-new-generator sandwiches over a base subalgebra `B`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_gen_gen_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_gen_gen_gt","kind":"theorem","line":495,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L495-L516","doc":"Descending pair: `k < m`. Cyclicity rotates `g k` to the **front**, where it\nmerges with `a` inside `H m`; T3 at level `m` then peels `g m`.\n\nThis is the case the ascending-word theorem\n(`MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_stabWord_eq_prod_tr`) cannot reach, and it is the\nsmallest instance showing that *descent by itself* is not the obstruction —\nrepetition is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_gen_gen_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_gen_gen_lt","kind":"theorem","line":482,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L482-L493","doc":"Ascending pair: `m < k`, so `g m ∈ H k` and T3 at level `k` peels directly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_adjoin_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_adjoin_gen","kind":"theorem","line":420,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L420-L440","doc":"**The disjoint-block law for the whole subalgebra generated by `g n`.**\n\nStrictly generalises `tr_mul_gpow`, and needs no `TwoSidedMarkov` hypothesis —\n`T.markov` is applied directly. This is the largest `b`-set for which the law is\nproved here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.adjoin_gen_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.adjoin_gen_affine","kind":"theorem","line":395,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L395-L418","doc":"Under the quadratic relation, every element of `Algebra.adjoin R {g n}` is\naffine in `g n`. The multiplicative step is where the relation earns its place:\n`(u + v·g)(u' + v'·g)` has a `g²` term, and `hq` folds it back down. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_gen_comb_of_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_gen_comb_of_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L376-L386","doc":"With the quadratic relation in force, `z'` is not independent\n(`OcneanuTrace.markovParam_inv_eq_sub`: `z' = z - h`), so every bond factor is a\ncombination of `z` and `h` alone. This is the form in which the measurement's\n\"no free parameter\" reading is visible: two ring elements, `z` and `h`, generate\nall three factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_gen_add_ginv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_gen_add_ginv","kind":"theorem","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L368-L374","doc":"The `pn` bond, without division: `c = c' = 1` in `tr_mul_gen_comb`. The\nmeasured factor is half of this, and halving is the reader's step rather than a\nhypothesis on the ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_gen_comb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_gen_comb","kind":"theorem","line":338,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L338-L366","doc":"**The mixed-crossing case: an arbitrary combination of the two generators.**\n\n`tr (a * (c • g n + c' • ginv n)) = tr a * (c * z + c' * z')` for `a ∈ H n`.\n\nMotivated by a measurement, not by symmetry. `computations/probes/\nbond_product_order_three_probe.py` expands the atom word's interface factors as\n`ε`-series to order 3 and finds all three to be **exactly** the two Markov\nparameters and their average — no offset and no free parameter:\n\n    pp   z             positive crossing        (c, c') = (1, 0)\n    pn   (z + z')/2    the average of the two   (c, c') = (1/2, 1/2)\n    nn   z'            negative crossing        (c, c') = (0, 1)\n\n`tr_mul_gen` and `tr_mul_geninv` already covered the two like-bonds; the mixed\nbond had no counterpart, and this supplies it for all three at once. The\nstatement is deliberately in `c • g + c' • ginv` rather than `(g + ginv)/2` so\nthat it needs **no** division and no hypothesis on `2 : R` — the caller supplies\nthe coefficients, and `R` stays a bare `CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.twoSidedMarkov_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.twoSidedMarkov_unit","kind":"instance","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L318-L336","doc":"**The new class is INHABITED — the anti-vacuity witness.**\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-tax, a content-bearing class that nothing can satisfy is worse\nthan no class at all: every `[TwoSidedMarkov T]`-conditional theorem below would\nbe vacuously true. `OcneanuTrace.unitMarkovTrace` — the one-dimensional tower\nover `R` with generator a fixed unit — satisfies it, because `R` is commutative\nand the trace is the identity, so `x * u * y = u * (x * y)` is `mul_comm`.\n\nThis is a *witness*, not evidence that the Hecke-tower Markov trace satisfies the\naxiom. That is the content of `qou-301d` and is not claimed here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_gpow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_gpow","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L299-L316","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.gpow_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.gpow_affine","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L279-L297","doc":"**The `g n`-power case**, from the two-sided axiom and the quadratic relation.\n\n`g n ^ e` is the \"run\" of `MonotoneWordFactorizes.runCoeff`; this states the\ndisjoint-block law for that family, which is the case the interleaved atom word\nneeds *within* one nucleon and which the ascending-word theorem cannot reach. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_geninv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_geninv","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L271-L277","doc":"The same for the inverse generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_gen","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L259-L269","doc":"**The single-generator case**, from the two-sided axiom.\n\n`tr (a * g n) = tr a * tr (g n)` for `a ∈ H n`. Note `tr (g n) = z` by T3 at\n`a = 1`, so this is T3 rewritten in the product form the disjoint-block law\nasserts — the smallest non-trivial instance of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_one_case","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.tr_mul_one_case","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L252-L257","doc":"**The `b ∈ H n` case, unconditionally.** When the second factor is already at\nor below the block's own level, the law is not about disjointness at all — it is\nthe statement that `tr` is multiplicative there, which is FALSE in general. So\nthis records the one sub-case that does hold with no hypothesis: `b = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.twoSidedMarkov_of_markovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.twoSidedMarkov_of_markovTrace","kind":"instance","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L242-L250","doc":"**Every `MarkovTrace` is a `TwoSidedMarkov`.** With this instance the class\ncarries no hypothesis: every `[TwoSidedMarkov T]` binder in this file is\ndischarged automatically, so those theorems are **unconditional**.\n\nThis is the opposite of what the file originally claimed, and it does **not**\nclose the gap below — see `TwoSidedImpliesDisjoint`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.markov_inv₂_of_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.markov_inv₂_of_markov","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L232-L240","doc":"The same for the negative generator, from T3'. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.markov₂_of_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.markov₂_of_markov","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L220-L230","doc":"**The two-sided form follows from the one-sided form.** Cyclicity moves `y`\nto the front, where it merges with `x` inside the subalgebra `H n`; T3 then\napplies to the single element `y * x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.markov_inv_of_twoSided","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.markov_inv_of_twoSided","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L206-L211","doc":"The same for the negative generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.markov_of_twoSided","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.markov_of_twoSided","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L193-L204","doc":"**T3 is the `y = 1` case of the two-sided form.**\n\n🛑 The docstring here read *\"The new class is a genuine strengthening … the\ncontent is that the implication runs only this way.\"* **That is refuted by\n`markov₂_of_markov` below: the implication runs BOTH ways, and the converse is\nthe four-line proof.** This theorem is therefore not an anti-vacuity check — it\nis one half of an equivalence, and the half that was already known. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.TwoSidedMarkov.markov_inv₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.TwoSidedMarkov.markov_inv₂","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L190-L190","doc":"Two-sided stabilisation by the negative generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.TwoSidedMarkov.markov₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.TwoSidedMarkov.markov₂","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L187-L187","doc":"Two-sided stabilisation by the positive generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.TwoSidedMarkov.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.TwoSidedMarkov.mk","kind":"ctor","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L185-L185","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.TwoSidedMarkov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.TwoSidedMarkov","kind":"class","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L161-L191","doc":"**The two-sided Markov property.**\n\n🛑 **CORRECTED 2026-09-07. This was introduced as \"the one input `MarkovTrace`\ndoes not carry\" and as a \"genuine strengthening\". BOTH CLAIMS ARE FALSE, and\nthey were mine.** `markov₂_of_markov` below derives this property from\n`tr_mul_comm` (T1) and `markov` (T3) alone, in four lines, and\n`twoSidedMarkov_of_markovTrace` makes it a global instance — so **every**\n`MarkovTrace` satisfies it and the class carries no hypothesis at all.\n\nThe derivation is a one-liner once seen, which is why the error is worth\nrecording rather than quietly deleting: `H n` is a **`Subalgebra`**, so it is\nclosed under multiplication, and cyclicity moves the right-hand factor around to\njoin the left one —\n\n    tr (x * g n * y) = tr (y * (x * g n)) = tr ((y * x) * g n)\n                     = z * tr (y * x)     = z * tr (x * y)\n\nwith `y * x ∈ H n` the only structural input. Nothing about the ordering of a\nword, nothing two-sided, and no new axiom: the \"two-sided\" form is the one-sided\nform conjugated.\n\nThe class is kept because it names the standard Ocneanu conditional-expectation\nproperty and downstream statements read better for it — **not** because anything\nneeds to assume it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.DisjointBlockMultiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.DisjointBlockMultiplicative","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L154-L159","doc":"**The disjoint-block trace law**, as a `Prop` about `T`.\n\nStated rather than proved: see the module docstring. This is the property the\nmeasured bond product of the atom word is the arithmetic shadow of. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.ginv_mem_shifted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.ginv_mem_shifted","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L150-L152","doc":"Every inverse generator at level `≥ n` is in `shifted n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.g_mem_shifted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.g_mem_shifted","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L146-L148","doc":"Every generator at level `≥ n` is in `shifted n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.shifted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTrace.shifted","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DisjointBlockTraceLaw.lean#L136-L144","doc":"The **shifted subalgebra** at level `n`: generated by every generator, and\nevery inverse generator, at level `n` or above.\n\nThis is the algebraic stand-in for \"the strands to the right of block `n`\". It is\ndeliberately *not* `H n`'s complement or commutant — no commutation is assumed\nanywhere in this file, because the disjoint-block law is about the trace, not\nabout the algebra. ","signatureChunk":0}]}